WEBVTT

00:01.200 --> 00:06.010
After continuous fierce fights, the climax of the Kalos League is finally about to begin.

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:07.190 --> 00:12.290
Let's have the two Trainers who've won their way to these glorious finals enter the stadium!

00:13.690 --> 00:15.040
Satoshi!

00:16.690 --> 00:17.850
Alan!

00:23.140 --> 00:24.620
Alan, do your best!

00:30.730 --> 00:31.510
It's time.

00:32.550 --> 00:33.540
Alan is strong.

00:34.180 --> 00:35.330
Let's go all out!

00:36.100 --> 00:37.380
I've been looking forward to...

00:38.140 --> 00:39.710
...fighting you here.

00:40.620 --> 00:41.520
But I won't let you...

00:42.180 --> 00:42.850
...have this match!

00:43.930 --> 00:46.240
This is the field for the finals!

00:48.590 --> 00:50.620
It's the rock/water field!

00:56.270 --> 01:01.990
The Finals!
Satoshi VS Alan!!

01:02.850 --> 01:06.000
Who will be crowned with the laurels of victory? Will it be Satoshi...

01:06.180 --> 01:06.820
...or will it be Alan?

01:07.710 --> 01:09.010
The fight begins...

01:09.380 --> 01:09.830
...now!

01:11.190 --> 01:14.880
The battle between Satoshi and Alan will now take place.

01:15.880 --> 01:17.140
You may use six Pokémon each.

01:17.620 --> 01:18.980
Pokémon may be substituted freely.

01:19.670 --> 01:23.570
As soon as either party's Pokémon are all unable to battle, the battle is over.

01:21.010 --> 01:30.850
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:21.010 --> 01:30.850
Z

01:24.180 --> 01:29.420
Also, once one side only has three Pokémon left, there will be a change of battlefields.

01:29.970 --> 01:31.410
Both of you, please call out your Pokémon.

01:31.930 --> 01:33.650
Pikachu, I choose you!

01:37.710 --> 01:38.190
Come out,

01:38.670 --> 01:39.250
Bangiras!

01:48.730 --> 01:49.560
This is troublesome.

01:50.640 --> 01:53.080
So Alan has a Bangiras on hand as well.

01:53.880 --> 01:56.060
The Sandstorm is caused by its Ability, Sand Stream.

01:56.430 --> 01:59.070
He is trying to restrict Pikachu's field of vision as well as its movements.

01:59.500 --> 02:00.020
It'll be fine.

02:00.460 --> 02:01.780
This is Satoshi; he'll fight his way through.

02:02.110 --> 02:03.160
Do your best, Satoshi!

02:03.430 --> 02:04.840
Do your best, Pikachu!

02:06.150 --> 02:07.930
Now then, begin the battle!

02:09.240 --> 02:10.110
Let's go, Alan!

02:10.770 --> 02:11.640
Come at us!

02:15.150 --> 02:15.680
Bangiras,

02:16.010 --> 02:16.800
Dark Pulse!

02:19.230 --> 02:20.350
Dodge, Pikachu!

02:24.540 --> 02:24.950
That's it!

02:25.410 --> 02:27.410
Pikachu, use Iron Tail on the water!

02:34.390 --> 02:35.250
Thunderbolt!

02:39.120 --> 02:39.500
Not bad.

02:43.960 --> 02:44.890
All right!

02:44.890 --> 02:47.130
I cannot believe it wiped out Sandstorm by spraying water on it!

02:47.670 --> 02:51.150
Not only that, but they instantly followed it up with an Electric move while Bangiras was drenched.

02:51.390 --> 02:52.140
Amazing.

02:54.260 --> 02:55.310
We're not done yet.

02:56.190 --> 02:57.020
Electro Ball!

03:02.340 --> 03:03.310
Stone Edge!

03:06.560 --> 03:07.320
Hit them with your tail!

03:11.800 --> 03:13.120
Send them back with Iron Tail!

03:17.420 --> 03:18.130
Aim at where it will land!

03:18.490 --> 03:19.190
Crunch!

03:22.160 --> 03:23.000
Iron Tail!

03:29.290 --> 03:30.470
Now, use Electro Ball!

03:39.330 --> 03:40.560
Bangiras is unable to battle!

03:40.980 --> 03:42.020
Pikachu wins!

03:43.300 --> 03:45.470
Those were excellent consecutive attacks!

03:45.610 --> 03:48.590
Satoshi has had a promising start!

03:49.100 --> 03:50.900
That's one victory for us so far!

03:52.980 --> 03:54.050
Yay!

03:54.700 --> 03:56.300
He's impressing right from the start.

03:56.550 --> 03:59.420
Getting the first victory gives him an advantage for later on.

04:00.080 --> 04:02.170
If he defeats the remaining five, he will win the league!

04:02.530 --> 04:05.360
Since the semifinals, Satoshi-kun has been on a roll.

04:05.690 --> 04:06.000
Yes.

04:11.460 --> 04:12.670
I can't go back right now.

04:13.970 --> 04:15.160
I've lost even more now than...

04:15.740 --> 04:17.100
...I had before I set off on my journey.

04:18.410 --> 04:19.800
Until I get it back...

04:21.180 --> 04:22.120
That's another reason why I...

04:22.680 --> 04:23.900
...have to get much stronger.

04:30.600 --> 04:31.080
Alan...

04:31.670 --> 04:33.280
What burden are you carrying?

04:34.900 --> 04:38.070
The excitement inside the stadium for the Kalos League finals is extraordinarily high.

04:39.010 --> 04:41.710
However, the fight has only just begun.

04:42.340 --> 04:43.230
All right, cut!

04:43.450 --> 04:44.520
All right, let's go to the next spot.

04:45.270 --> 04:45.790
Okay.

04:46.530 --> 04:48.930
This will be a harsh battle, no doubt about it.

04:49.340 --> 04:51.780
All the Pokémon will get completely exhausted.

04:52.000 --> 04:54.610
Once they're tired out, we'll take them.

04:55.050 --> 04:56.470
That's a perfect plan.

04:56.770 --> 04:59.390
We'll get the league winner's and the runner-up's Pokémon...

04:59.390 --> 05:01.710
...<i>and</i> that Pikachu on top of it,

05:01.710 --> 05:03.850
which will make us an unbeatable Rocket Gang!

05:04.510 --> 05:05.960
Hey, what are you doing?!

05:06.540 --> 05:08.100
Sorry!

05:10.620 --> 05:12.030
Well done, Pikachu.

05:12.270 --> 05:13.120
Take a rest.

05:14.900 --> 05:16.510
Onvern, I choose you!

05:20.030 --> 05:21.070
This sensation is...

05:21.670 --> 05:22.680
...what I've been waiting for.

05:23.160 --> 05:24.270
Go, Manyula!

05:28.690 --> 05:31.640
The next matchup is Manyula against Onvern!

05:32.650 --> 05:34.070
Onvern, Supersonic!

05:37.440 --> 05:37.970
Manyula,

05:38.120 --> 05:38.510
Protect!

05:42.390 --> 05:42.770
Night Slash!

05:48.700 --> 05:49.230
Supersonic!

05:54.740 --> 05:55.450
Ice Beam!

05:57.130 --> 05:57.910
Boomburst!

06:03.280 --> 06:04.080
Dragon Claw!

06:11.230 --> 06:11.740
Double Team!

06:14.400 --> 06:16.220
Use Supersonic to find the real one!

06:21.230 --> 06:21.890
There!

06:23.440 --> 06:23.810
Dodge!

06:27.190 --> 06:27.980
Ice Beam!

06:29.640 --> 06:29.940
Dodge!

06:38.600 --> 06:39.600
Night Slash!

06:52.540 --> 06:55.170
Onvern is unable to battle. Manyula wins!

06:55.860 --> 06:59.680
Aiming an Ice Beam at its opponent's wings earned Manyula the victory!

06:59.880 --> 07:00.650
Onvern!

07:02.910 --> 07:04.320
Are you all right, Onvern?

07:14.000 --> 07:15.740
Onvern, take a good rest.

07:17.300 --> 07:19.110
All right. I'm counting on you, Luchabull.

07:22.650 --> 07:23.290
Onvern...

07:23.910 --> 07:25.600
Now he evened the score again.

07:25.910 --> 07:26.430
It'll be fine.

07:27.320 --> 07:28.960
Luchabull will avenge it!

07:29.360 --> 07:30.790
Luchabull, let's go!

07:35.790 --> 07:36.510
Luchabull,

07:36.510 --> 07:37.550
Karate Chop!

07:39.190 --> 07:39.630
Dodge!

07:43.510 --> 07:45.160
Luchabull attacks viciously!

07:45.160 --> 07:47.600
Dodging is all Manyula can do!

07:48.750 --> 07:51.930
Fighting type moves are super effective against Manyula.

07:52.220 --> 07:53.070
That was a nice attack.

07:53.340 --> 07:55.120
However, that only applies when it hits.

07:55.770 --> 07:57.510
Manyula sees through everything it does.

08:00.620 --> 08:00.990
Now!

08:01.370 --> 08:02.870
Aim Ice Beam under Luchabull's feet!

08:09.650 --> 08:10.900
An ice field, huh...?

08:13.620 --> 08:14.750
Fire an Ice Beam!

08:16.990 --> 08:17.510
Block it!

08:26.190 --> 08:27.140
Manyula, Night Slash!

08:28.800 --> 08:29.270
It's not over yet!

08:37.970 --> 08:38.690
That was well done.

08:38.690 --> 08:41.240
It lessened the damage by using the ice to its advantage.

08:41.590 --> 08:42.750
Send it flying into the rocks!

08:43.090 --> 08:43.320
Night Slash!

08:45.440 --> 08:46.080
It's not over yet.

08:52.940 --> 08:54.650
Manyula's attacks are vicious!

08:54.650 --> 08:56.510
Has Luchabull been driven into a corner?!

08:57.730 --> 08:58.830
No, it's standing!

08:59.120 --> 09:01.260
Luchabull is still standing!

09:05.200 --> 09:08.650
Luchabull gets pumped as it takes hits from its opponent.

09:09.710 --> 09:11.060
This time <i>we'll</i> take the offensive!

09:11.790 --> 09:12.880
Bring it on.

09:13.180 --> 09:13.900
Night Slash!

09:15.860 --> 09:16.980
Luchabull, go!

09:23.790 --> 09:25.300
Now, use Flying Press!

09:38.630 --> 09:39.850
Manyula is unable to battle!

09:40.340 --> 09:41.340
Luchabull wins!

09:41.710 --> 09:42.610
All right!

09:44.420 --> 09:48.500
Luchabull has achieved a turnaround victory with a fierce aerial assault!

09:49.360 --> 09:50.530
I expected nothing less from Luchabull.

09:50.840 --> 09:53.510
Satoshi made full use of Luchabull's fighting style.

09:54.000 --> 09:57.480
Luchabull believes in Satoshi and Satoshi believes in Luchabull.

09:57.680 --> 09:58.110
That's right.

09:58.880 --> 10:01.870
After all, that's Satoshi's greatest weapon.

10:02.740 --> 10:04.110
They're all good Pokémon.

10:04.850 --> 10:05.280
Alan,

10:05.940 --> 10:06.660
do your best.

10:07.140 --> 10:07.700
Come out,

10:08.020 --> 10:08.700
Kirikizan!

10:13.500 --> 10:16.380
Alan's third is Kirikizan!

10:17.190 --> 10:18.740
Brace yourself, Luchabull!

10:20.340 --> 10:20.890
Thunder Wave!

10:26.240 --> 10:26.870
Luchabull!

10:27.490 --> 10:32.180
Kirikizan's Thunder Wave has turned the situation dire for Luchabull, which was already damaged from the last battle!

10:32.180 --> 10:33.280
Get up, Luchabull!

10:36.860 --> 10:37.720
Guillotine!

10:38.730 --> 10:39.750
X-Scissor!

10:48.800 --> 10:50.120
Luchabull, High Jump Kick!

10:54.380 --> 10:54.750
Dodge!

11:00.620 --> 11:01.460
Guillotine!

11:12.670 --> 11:15.340
Luchabull is unable to battle! Kirikizan wins!

11:15.790 --> 11:20.080
There it is! Guillotine, which knocks the opponent out in one hit!

11:20.510 --> 11:22.190
Satoshi was the first to defeat two Pokémon,

11:22.730 --> 11:24.190
so I thought he had the advantage, but...

11:24.570 --> 11:26.110
...Alan recovered immediately.

11:26.560 --> 11:27.110
I have got to hand it to him.

11:28.890 --> 11:30.220
You did your best, Luchabull.

11:30.690 --> 11:31.580
Take a good rest.

11:33.430 --> 11:36.710
Battling Satoshi really is fun.

11:37.460 --> 11:39.000
He makes me forget time.

11:39.880 --> 11:40.840
I want to enjoy this without having to think about anything else...

11:41.470 --> 11:43.090
...for just a little bit longer.

11:43.900 --> 11:44.320
Go,

11:44.670 --> 11:45.210
Kenhallow!

11:48.820 --> 11:50.210
I'm counting on you, Fiarrow!

12:05.330 --> 12:06.120
Steel Wing!

12:15.990 --> 12:17.750
Both of them clashed against the other!

12:19.410 --> 12:20.040
Flame Charge!

12:26.170 --> 12:27.310
Sky Attack!

12:37.870 --> 12:38.690
Air Slash!

12:44.650 --> 12:45.520
Evade it, Fiarrow!

12:55.370 --> 12:57.440
Let's raise your speed! Flame Charge!

12:59.710 --> 13:00.480
Dodge!

13:05.430 --> 13:06.350
Sky Attack!

13:10.100 --> 13:10.870
Fiarrow,

13:10.870 --> 13:11.680
Brave Bird!

13:20.850 --> 13:23.510
Brave Bird and Sky Attack clash!

13:26.350 --> 13:27.070
What happened?

13:29.580 --> 13:30.440
Fiarrow!

13:31.600 --> 13:34.200
Fiarrow and Kenhallow are both unable to battle!

13:35.380 --> 13:39.780
The duel in the skies ended with a double knockout!

13:44.430 --> 13:45.560
Pokémon Quiz.

13:45.770 --> 13:46.780
The answer is...?

13:48.960 --> 13:59.000
Coming up next:

13:48.960 --> 13:53.930
The final match becomes even more heated!

13:49.870 --> 13:54.600
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

13:53.960 --> 13:59.000
Pikachu faces one tough opponent after another!

14:07.150 --> 14:11.330
Since they're both down to three Pokémon, there will now be a field change.

14:12.460 --> 14:13.300
Three on three.

14:13.990 --> 14:16.800
The finals have turned into yet another fight where neither party is inferior to the other.

14:17.150 --> 14:19.190
One slight mistake will change the tide entirely.

14:19.800 --> 14:20.960
That is the kind of battle they are having.

14:21.430 --> 14:21.890
Yeah.

14:22.400 --> 14:23.880
It even makes <i>me</i> anxious.

14:24.150 --> 14:27.840
Satoshi has never won against Alan before.

14:27.840 --> 14:28.170
What?

14:29.140 --> 14:30.490
He's that strong?

14:31.030 --> 14:32.760
But that was the Satoshi of the past.

14:33.900 --> 14:36.760
Satoshi is stronger now than he was back then.

14:37.330 --> 14:38.380
Three left...

14:42.890 --> 14:44.930
Yeah, I've got you guys.

14:45.200 --> 14:47.540
And you guys have got me.

14:49.560 --> 14:50.110
Alan,

14:50.560 --> 14:52.100
let's enjoy this till the end!

14:55.080 --> 14:55.850
It's your eyes.

14:56.580 --> 14:58.750
Your eyes stir up my fighting spirit.

14:59.680 --> 15:00.400
That's why I'm...

15:00.950 --> 15:02.030
...so fixated on you.

15:04.550 --> 15:05.630
Alan is smiling.

15:06.530 --> 15:08.010
I've never seen him like that.

15:08.870 --> 15:09.490
I see.

15:10.510 --> 15:11.130
Put it into action.

15:12.370 --> 15:14.550
Before long, the finals will reach their climax and...

15:15.320 --> 15:15.960
...all of Kalos...

15:16.350 --> 15:20.080
...no, the whole <i>world</i> will focus on Miare City.

15:21.630 --> 15:24.180
The field for the second half of the Kalos League finals is...

15:24.650 --> 15:26.310
...the meadow field!

15:26.670 --> 15:31.160
How will this field change influence the fight?

15:32.000 --> 15:33.150
Both of you, please call out your Pokémon!

15:33.450 --> 15:35.230
Pikachu, I choose you!

15:38.990 --> 15:39.440
Come out,

15:39.770 --> 15:40.520
Metagross!

15:44.950 --> 15:50.280
Satoshi chooses Pikachu once more, while Alan counters with Metagross!

15:51.470 --> 15:51.930
Begin...

15:52.520 --> 15:53.170
...the battle!

15:53.640 --> 15:55.690
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

15:58.110 --> 15:58.880
Agility!

16:04.990 --> 16:05.720
Keep your distance!

16:07.780 --> 16:08.310
Corner it!

16:11.630 --> 16:12.270
Metal Claw!

16:17.200 --> 16:17.890
Rock Slide!

16:22.660 --> 16:23.350
Pikachu!

16:33.710 --> 16:34.820
Good job, Pikachu!

16:36.800 --> 16:37.560
Meteor Mash!

16:48.600 --> 16:49.270
Pikachu!

16:52.880 --> 16:56.330
The fact that we'll be able to get such a strong Metagross is absolutely perfect.

16:56.800 --> 17:02.070
But seeing the Pikachu that always beats us to a pulp getting pummeled itself...

17:02.310 --> 17:04.030
...makes me feel a bit conflicted.

17:04.530 --> 17:06.080
It doesn't matter who wins, does it?

17:06.430 --> 17:07.830
After all, we'll be getting all of them together!

17:08.510 --> 17:10.580
Well, yeah, but...

17:14.070 --> 17:14.670
Let's finish this!

17:15.000 --> 17:15.750
Meteor Mash!

17:17.800 --> 17:18.750
Hang in there, Pikachu!

17:19.120 --> 17:19.960
Electro Ball!

17:27.200 --> 17:27.710
What?!

17:28.030 --> 17:30.270
Pikachu stands its ground!

17:30.430 --> 17:31.430
Jump onto Metagross!

17:36.130 --> 17:36.650
Shake it off!

17:40.270 --> 17:42.050
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

17:45.590 --> 17:47.970
An unexpected Thunderbolt from Pikachu!

17:47.970 --> 17:50.060
Will Metagross be able to endure this?

17:51.260 --> 17:54.340
With Pikachu on its back, Metagross cannot even attack it.

17:54.340 --> 17:58.000
Now it is a matter of whether Metagross will go down first or whether Pikachu gets shaken off first.

17:58.480 --> 18:00.020
Hang in there, Pikachu!

18:02.980 --> 18:04.860
Metagross has staggered!

18:04.860 --> 18:07.050
Thunderbolt is affecting it!

18:07.640 --> 18:08.560
Metagross!

18:17.340 --> 18:17.880
Pikachu,

18:18.160 --> 18:19.030
Iron Tail!

18:27.210 --> 18:29.530
Metagross is unable to battle. Pikachu wins!

18:30.110 --> 18:31.030
All right!

18:32.260 --> 18:34.060
Pikachu's attack completely reversed the situation!

18:34.270 --> 18:36.900
Its turnaround victory was brilliant!

18:38.700 --> 18:40.150
All right, all right!

18:40.150 --> 18:41.360
Now it's three-to-two!

18:41.360 --> 18:41.630
Yes.

18:41.980 --> 18:42.670
He's recovered!

18:43.470 --> 18:44.400
But his opponent is Alan...

18:44.850 --> 18:45.920
It is too early to relax.

18:46.500 --> 18:48.510
Pikachu has suffered a lot of damage as well.

18:48.820 --> 18:50.370
What a surprise.

18:50.370 --> 18:52.230
He doesn't give up on a fight until the last second.

18:52.720 --> 18:54.270
This is a victory as only Satoshi-kun can achieve it.

18:54.850 --> 18:55.540
All right!

18:56.490 --> 18:56.770
Excuse me?

18:57.440 --> 18:59.990
Uh, well… If it doesn't matter who wins,

19:00.310 --> 19:02.690
I might as well root for the brat boy...

19:02.690 --> 19:03.090
Just a thought...

19:08.450 --> 19:08.910
Go,

19:09.290 --> 19:10.080
Lizardon!

19:15.430 --> 19:16.410
He's using Lizardon <i>now?</i>

19:27.460 --> 19:29.930
All right, we're only going to do better from now on!

19:31.420 --> 19:32.420
Quick Attack!

19:38.840 --> 19:40.170
Thunderbolt!

19:43.540 --> 19:45.670
A Quick Attack followed by Thunderbolt!

19:45.670 --> 19:47.250
Pikachu is using swift attacks!

19:48.480 --> 19:49.970
It's working... It's working!

19:51.140 --> 19:53.790
Thunderbolt is super effective against Lizardon!

20:04.720 --> 20:05.160
Satoshi...

20:05.950 --> 20:06.440
Pikachu...

20:06.760 --> 20:07.300
Do your best!

20:08.780 --> 20:09.380
Pikachu...

20:09.710 --> 20:10.340
...or Lizardon?

20:10.910 --> 20:13.920
Who will the goddess of victory side with?

20:14.760 --> 20:17.850
How will the battle between Satoshi and Alan go?

20:18.860 --> 20:22.050
The heated final match still continues on!

20:26.150 --> 20:28.330
The passionate and exciting points of the Pokémon movie!

20:28.570 --> 20:29.620
Get blown away!

20:31.000 --> 21:21.030
The blockbuster is
currently in theaters!

20:31.060 --> 20:34.670
AZOTH
KINGDOM

20:31.470 --> 20:34.480
The setting of the story is the Azoth Kingdom.

20:34.670 --> 20:38.080
The Genius Scientist

20:34.670 --> 20:38.080
ELIPHAS

20:35.000 --> 20:41.130
It is a city of super ingenuity that Éliphas, the master of Mystery Science, built up with his knowledge and craft.

20:41.780 --> 20:44.010
Minister
JARVIS

20:41.950 --> 20:45.430
In order to rule over the kingdom, Jarvis, the minister of this country,

20:44.010 --> 20:45.550
Prince
RACEL

20:45.550 --> 20:47.050
Jarvis' underlings
ETHER DOGA

20:45.720 --> 20:46.990
uses Prince Racel.

20:47.550 --> 20:51.560
His target was Magearna, the greatest invention created by Éliphas.

20:52.450 --> 20:57.090
What I need to fulfill my ideals is not Magearna, just the Soul Heart!

20:57.360 --> 20:58.800
Mega Wave!

21:00.170 --> 21:05.070
Jarvis proceeds with his plan by controlling a group of forcefully mega evolved Pokémon.

21:05.070 --> 21:06.740
Princess
CHYMIA

21:05.790 --> 21:11.660
And so, Princess Chymia challenges the Mega Evolution Army together with Satoshi and Volcanion!

21:12.000 --> 21:12.890
Chymia-sama...

21:13.510 --> 21:16.060
I have no need for you in my plan.

21:17.200 --> 21:19.900
Watch how this battle will turn out in the theater!

21:23.230 --> 21:25.110
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:25.310 --> 21:26.640
Towards our next adventure!

21:27.180 --> 21:28.260
Take this, Alan!

21:28.640 --> 21:30.050
